course: dictionary
lesson: 7749
title: Puncture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A puncture is a small hole made by something sharp. It is often used about a tyre, where the hole lets the air out. «A punctured tyre goes flat because the squashed air inside escapes through the hole.» Flat means the tyre has lost its air, so punctured must describe the hole that caused it.
explain: The word can also be a verb. «Tyres often get punctured by thorns and nails.» Here punctured means had a small hole made in it. Look at the words around it: thorns and nails are sharp things, so they make the holes.
explain: Puncture can also describe your body. A puncture wound is a deep, small wound made by something pointed, like a nail. «Puncture» and «punctured» are the same word family. You can check any new word by swapping in your meaning: a small hole made by something sharp fits every sentence here.
fact: A puncture is a small hole made by something sharp.
fact: «Puncture» can be a noun (a puncture) or a verb (to puncture something).
fact: «Punctured» means had a small hole made in it.
fact: A puncture wound is a deep, small wound made by something pointed, like a nail.
fact: Puncture wounds from nails or animal bites need cleaning, and sometimes a doctor.
exercise: «A punctured tyre goes flat because the squashed air inside escapes through the hole.» What does punctured mean here? | *Had a small hole made in it, so air leaks out | Pumped up very hard | Covered in soapy water | Painted bright red
exercise: Tomas says a puncture is a loud crash on the road. What is a puncture really? | A type of bread | A loud bang like a crash | *A small hole made by something sharp | A bicycle bell
exercise: «Tyres often get punctured by thorns and nails.» Which thing can puncture a tyre? | A soft pillow | Sunshine | *A thorn | A song
test: «In soapy water the air escaping from a punctured tube makes bubbles that show where the hole is.» What do the bubbles show? | *Where the puncture is | How fast you can ride | Where the bike is parked | The colour of the tube
test: What does «mend a puncture» mean? | Paint the tyre | *Fix the small hole so the tube holds air again | Ride very fast | Buy a new bike
exam: In first aid, what is a puncture wound? | A long, shallow scratch on the skin | *A deep, small wound made by something pointed, like a nail | A large cut from a broken window | A bruise that turns blue
